Python <pre><code>def chat_main(self, topic="General"):
    """Run the chat REPL loop."""

    path = self.make_chat_groups(topic, CHAT_DIR_NAME)

    while True:
        line = HelperFunctions().ask_for_input(self.callSign).strip()

        if line in ("/H", "/h"):
            HelperFunctions().choose_menu(CHAT, "Help menu")
        elif line in ("/U", "/u"):
            self.show_users()
        elif line == "/t" or line == "/T":
            self.list_chat_groups()
        elif line.startswith("/t ") or line.startswith("/T "):
            topic = line[3:].strip()
            path = self.make_chat_groups(topic, CHAT_DIR_NAME)
            sys.stdout.write("Now you are in " + topic + " chat!\r\n")
            sys.stdout.flush()
        elif line in ("/b", "/B"):
            return
        elif line in ("/m", "/M"):
            self.show_messages(path, topic)
        elif line.startswith("/"):
            print("Invalid command")
        else:
            self.write_file(path, line)
</code></pre> <p>Purpose: This is the core chat REPL loop.</p> <p>Command handling flow:</p> <ul> <li><code>/H</code> → show help</li> <li><code>/U</code> → show users</li> <li><code>/T</code> → list topics</li> <li><code>/T name</code> → join/create topic</li> <li><code>/M</code> → show messages</li> <li><code>/B</code> → exit chat</li> <li><code>text</code> → broadcast message</li> </ul> <p>LinBPQ Equivalent: This function is effectively a node port handler.</p>

